      "body": "## Motivation\n\n- An MLA draft (EAGLE, NEXTN, STANDALONE) on aiter with `--dcp-size > 1` crashes at startup with an opaque `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'shape'` in `forward_extend`.\n- Cause: the draft keeps a replicated KV pool, but the MLA model code still routes its extend through the DCP decode branch without the step's keys. The aiter extend cannot run that.\n- Users get no hint that the configuration is unsupported or what to change.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `AiterAttnBackend._reject_mla_draft_under_dcp` raises a clear `ValueError` when the backend is built, like the other `_reject_*` guards.\n- It reads `hf_config` only after the cheap checks, so targets and test fakes without `hf_config` are unaffected.\n- The CPU unit test `test/registered/unit/layers/attention/test_aiter_mla_draft_dcp_guard.py` pins the guard.\n\n| Case | Result |\n|---|---|\n| MLA draft, DCP > 1, KV replicated | `ValueError`: use `--dcp-size 1` or a non-MLA draft |\n| ROCm DSA draft (shards KV like the target) | allowed |\n| Target model, non-MLA draft (e.g. DSpark MHA), DCP 1 | unaffected |\n\n- Not covered: the check runs after weights load; drafts on another attention backend; real support, which needs the draft at DCP 1 in the model, the backend and the pool.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nDeepSeek-V2-Lite-Chat as its own STANDALONE draft, TP2, fp8 KV, aiter, MI355X. GSM8K: sgl-eval 0.1.3, 200 questions, greedy.\n\n| Setup | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| DCP2 | `AttributeError` at startup | `ValueError` with the message |\n| DCP1 | runs | runs: GSM8K 0.54, accept length 3.75 of 4 |\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\n- None: this only replaces a crash with an error.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). No user-facing change.\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n`pytest test/registered/unit/layers/attention/test_aiter_mla_draft_dcp_guard.py`: 3 passed. pre-commit passes.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41795402644](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41795402644)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41795402638](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41795402638)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41795402657](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41795402657)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
